# rally:ignore:start
# Generated by `rally init`. Lines between these markers are
# regenerated on every run — put your own rules OUTSIDE them.
#
# Every entry below is derived, a lock, or a cache: rally rebuilds it
# from `.rally/log/` on the next open. The canonical ledger (`log/`,
# `archive/`) and the self-description (`manifest.json`) are
# deliberately NOT listed — those are meant to be committed.

# Derived SQLite projection of the ledger, plus the WAL/SHM sidecars
# sqlite writes beside it and any copy `rally doctor` quarantines.
# Rebuilt by replay on the next open.
facts.db
facts.db-shm
facts.db-wal
facts.db.corrupt.*

# Advisory lock files. A kernel flock is scoped to the host that took
# it, so a committed lock names a machine nobody else has.
mutation.lock
session-reservation.lock
*.owner.lock

# rallyd runtime: its Unix socket, the address sidecar peers resolve
# it through, the pidfile, and the daemon log.
rallyd.sock
rallyd.sock.addr
rallyd.pid
rallyd.log

# Derived caches and per-tool read cursors — local reading position
# and fold results, never history.
cursors.json
watch-cursor.json
claim-index.json
.reconcile-cache.json
snapshot.cache.json

# Scratch from the write-to-temp-then-rename path; only ever present
# after a crash mid-write.
*.tmp-*
# rally:ignore:end
